Day 17 – Interactive Business Intelligence Dashboard using Dash

Objective

The objective of Day 17 was to develop an interactive Business Intelligence Dashboard using the Dash framework and Plotly. The dashboard provides real-time visualization of retail sales data, customer segmentation, and key business performance indicators to support data-driven decision-making.

Dataset Overview

The cleaned retail dataset (Year_2009_2010_Cleaned.csv) was imported for dashboard development. The dataset contains transaction details, customer information, sales values, and customer segmentation data.

Dataset Features

The dashboard utilizes the following features:

- Invoice
- Invoice Date
- Customer ID
- Customer Segment
- Quantity
- Price
- SalesAmount
- Year

These features were used to generate business metrics and interactive visualizations.

Data Preparation

The dataset was loaded using Pandas, and the Invoice Date column was converted into datetime format. A new Year feature was extracted from the Invoice Date to support year-wise analysis.

Dashboard Development

An interactive dashboard was developed using Dash and Plotly. The application provides a web-based interface for exploring business insights through charts and summary statistics.

Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

The following KPIs were calculated and displayed on the dashboard:

- Total Revenue
- Total Customers
- Total Orders
- Average Order Value

These metrics provide a quick overview of overall business performance.

Customer Segmentation Analysis

A donut chart was created to visualize the distribution of customers across different customer segments. This helps understand customer composition and purchasing behavior.

Revenue Analysis

A line chart was generated to display revenue trends over different years. This visualization highlights changes in business performance over time.

Customer Segment Revenue

A bar chart was created to compare revenue generated by different customer segments. This analysis identifies the customer groups contributing the most to overall sales.

Interactive Dashboard Interface

The dashboard was designed with a responsive layout using Dash components, including titles, KPI cards, charts, and interactive visualizations. Plotly charts provide dynamic exploration of business data.

Key Findings

• Successfully developed an interactive Business Intelligence Dashboard using Dash.
• Imported and prepared the cleaned retail dataset.
• Calculated Total Revenue, Total Customers, Total Orders, and Average Order Value.
• Created a customer segment distribution donut chart.
• Visualized yearly revenue trends using a line chart.
• Compared revenue across customer segments using a bar chart.
• Designed a responsive and interactive dashboard layout.
• Improved business insight visualization using Plotly charts.

Conclusion

Day 17 focused on developing an interactive Business Intelligence Dashboard using Dash and Plotly. The dashboard successfully presents key business metrics, customer segmentation, and revenue analysis through dynamic visualizations. This application provides an effective platform for monitoring retail performance and supports business intelligence, reporting, and strategic decision-making.